{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines","id":910040,"title":"So, remember the neat terminals from VtM - Bloodlines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-08T06:58:42-07:00","id":910040,"title":"So, remember the neat terminals from VtM - Bloodlines?","content":"I made something similar in Java for my Vampire: the Requiem troupe. It is basically a simulated pseudo-terminal, like a mini-game, running the Aegis Kai Doru's very own operating system <b>AkDOS</b>!<br /> <br /> The code is being released under the GPL 3.0 license (free and open-source, changes also need to be made open source). It runs without a gui, so it captures the look and feel of the terminal from Bloodlines nicely. Since the code will also be available, you could modify it yourself or ask me to modify it for use in your own chronicles. Plus, I'll be adding new features to the program, such as hacking mini-games and random interactions with God-Machines, ghosts, and evil spirits that might possess the terminal in an attempt to communicate with the user.<br /> <br /> Here's the github repo:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/armandosstyl/akdos\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/armandosstyl/akdos\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/armandosstyl/akdos\" target=\"_blank\"> https://github.com/armandosstyl/akdos </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The code will be up in the next few minutes, plus a build with instructions on how to run (needs Java Runtime Environment 1.8).<br /> Hope you wonderful people will like it and comment so I can improve both my coding and the program itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T17:43:49-07:00","id":910433,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://github.com/armandosstyl/akdos/tree/master/Builds/0.90a\" target=\"_blank\">A build for version 0.90a is now available for download</a><br /> <br /> Simply download AkDOS.jar from the link above (<b>View Raw</b> should do it), then follow the instructions from README.md<br /> and you'll be all set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:19:55-07:00","id":910811,"title":"","content":"I will totally check this out at home (on a work computer now). Love Bloodlines and am a programmer too, so lots of interest from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:02:30-07:00","id":911012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=910811#post910811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will totally check this out at home (on a work computer now). Love Bloodlines and am a programmer too, so lots of interest from me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! Let me know how it goes, it's my first program outside college projects so I wouldn't be surprised if I missed something or did not package the build properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key