 wrong when using GitHub Desktop for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:30:43-07:00","id":914425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=913853#post913853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpacked zip, run 'EXE', nothing came out. I checked system Task Manager, not seeing new processes.<br /> <br /> Side Question - <b>How do you operate now GitHub?</b> I cannot easily download ZIP file. Maybe I did something wrong when using GitHub Desktop for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you also unzip the jre folder? It needs to be extracted in the same folder as the EXE file to run.<br /> Just tested the program in another machine, it runs although Windows warned about <i>running an unknown application</i> or some security warning. Are downloaded exe files allowed to run in your machine?<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could unblock the file from the EXE file's properties.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/hD9hpQy.png?1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> On Github, you click on the <b>Akdos_090a_x64.zip</b> file, and then <b>View Raw</b>. That should download it for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:23:38-07:00","id":914901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=914425#post914425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you also unzip the jre folder? It needs to be extracted in the same folder as the EXE file to run.<br /> Just tested the program in another machine, it runs although Windows warned about <i>running an unknown application</i> or some security warning. Are downloaded exe files allowed to run in your machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could swear when I downloaded it few hours after your post there where no EXE file. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nonetheless - now it is and terminal works. Only it states it's version 0.22 and characters are white, not green. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Can I do something other than pinging my admin and sending distress call?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:27:27-07:00","id":915460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=914901#post914901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could swear when I downloaded it few hours after your post there where no EXE file. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, maybe the pull request on GitHub took a while to update. Next time I'll wait a couple of hours after the upload of new code/builds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=914901#post914901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonetheless - now it is and terminal works. Only it states it's version 0.22 and characters are white, not green. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the 0.22 version is the in-character version (sort of an easter egg for my tabletop troupe). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Starting from AkDOS 1.0, in and out-of-character versions will be the same.<br /> <br /> I used the Command Prompt for the interface for a more local, realistic feel to the terminal. Might change that in a future version, if users prefer something as close as possible to Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=914901#post914901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I do something other than pinging my admin and sending distress call?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the initial menu, go ahead and type the default username. It will then prompt you to type the password for that user (Antigoni).<br /> <br /> Default username: <b>A-DA 0609</b><br /> Default password: <b>drakolimni_1911</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 06-16-2016, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T02:25:07-07:00","id":915477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=915460#post915460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used the Command Prompt for the interface for a more local, realistic feel to the terminal. Might change that in a future version, if users prefer something as close as possible to Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just like old-school feel of green characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If it not a big request ( like line or two extra in code), maybe second variant of final version?<br /> <br /> Either way, I can go behind users Command Prompt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=915460#post915460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the initial menu, go ahead and type the default username. It will then prompt you to type the password for that user (Antigoni).<br /> <br /> Default username: <b>A-DA 0609</b><br /> Default password: <b>drakolimni_1911</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Will check later this weekend - now I swaped with work and my own two chronicles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:51:00-07:00","id":920953,"title":"","content":"Okay, tested today a bit and some thoughts. I generally like features. What I would make to app really shine:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Users configuration</b> - You get previously prepared data - like from XML or TXT file - and take usernames, password to it, maybe different variants of access on those. Basically so I could make one configuration file for my PCs group and run terminals on those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>Numerating lists </b>- As IT technician, I run a large of DOS programs. Those are made with numeration options like &quot;Choose option: 1- Search 2-Relics 3-Organization&quot;. And numbers assinged to options. Then you can use 'y' and 'n' as universal answers on yes/no questions in interface.</li> <li><b>Redesigning names and such</b> - you run <b>Hunter</b> game, I run <b>Mage</b> - much more logical for me would to use something like name 'Arcanet' instead of 'AkDoS', someone other to use vampires ones ( maybe 'Bloodlines' or some other name for Karthian soft ). I suspect it's only a problem to make texts based on variables names like 'Race1' and 'Faction1' and then loading particular XML file with configuration for Terminal that equal those to 'Vampires' and 'Circle of Crone', respectively. 5*5 model of CoD makes this not so difficult to program, I assume.</li> <li><b>Please, add e-mail accounts</b> - they were one of highlights of VTMB version. Cryptic massages send to characters in retro 'secured' soft. Could also make separate config file for those, so I could send to my PCs as ST.</li> <li><b>Auto-completion</b> - when I hit TAB commands are not autofilled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T07:14:01-07:00","id":929709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910040-so-remember-the-neat-terminals-from-vtm-bloodlines?p=920953#post920953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, tested today a bit and some thoughts. I generally like features. What I would make to app really shine:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Users configuration</b> - You get previously prepared data - like from XML or TXT file - and take usernames, password to it, maybe different variants of access on those. Basically so I could make one configuration file for my PCs group and run terminals on those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>Numerating lists </b>- As IT technician, I run a large of DOS programs. Those are made with numeration options like &quot;Choose option: 1- Search 2-Relics 3-Organization&quot;. And numbers assinged to options. Then you can use 'y' and 'n' as universal answers on yes/no questions in interface.</li> <li><b>Redesigning names and such</b> - you run <b>Hunter</b> game, I run <b>Mage</b> - much more logical for me would to use something like name 'Arcanet' instead of 'AkDoS', someone other to use vampires ones ( maybe 'Bloodlines' or some other name for Karthian soft ). I suspect it's only a problem to make texts based on variables names like 'Race1' and 'Faction1' and then loading particular XML file with configuration for Terminal that equal those to 'Vampires' and 'Circle of Crone', respectively. 5*5 model of CoD makes this not so difficult to program, I assume.</li> <li><b>Please, add e-mail accounts</b> - they were one of highlights of VTMB version. Cryptic massages send to characters in retro 'secured' soft. Could also make separate config file for those, so I could send to my PCs as ST.</li> <li><b>Auto-completion</b> - when I hit TAB commands are not autofilled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the input! I will be definitely implementing a lot of your suggestions, though I would like to focus on the rules side first. This means inputing characters' Attributes and Skills relevant to Hacking, and rolling to see if the hacking was successful -including a cumulative penalty for several attempts and a Dramatic Failure scenario. After this is done, I will be implementing your suggestions (because I really like them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:11:23-08:00","id":1008124,"title":"","content":"So, I've been toying around my original source code since releasing 0.9. The two major features I am in the process of adding, before releasing version 1.0 (hopefully during the weekend) are:<ul><li>Integrated dice roller (menu for inserting character stats, 10s re-rolled, successes calculated, successive attempts at -1, dramatic failures taken into account) for hacking. Not as fancy as the hacking sequence in Bloodlines, but it's important that this was done so I can later focus on moving away from a console-based app and into a gui that will resemble the terminal in Bloodlines. (100% completed)</li> <li>XML-based database. This will allow you to simply edit readable xml files to add or remove elements from the database. (25% completed)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:02:38-08:00","id":1008201,"title":"","content":"Waiting for the next big release then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:29:28-08:00","id":1008380,"title":"","content":"Worked overtime and finished version 1.0! You can find it on the same github page (<a href=\"https://github.com/armandosstyl/akdos/tree/master/Builds/1.00\" target=\"_blank\">or here if you don't want to scroll up</a>).<br /> <br /> New features include:<ul><li>Added hacking function. Users can enter their character's attribute and skill ratings to initiate hacking on the terminal.</li> <li>Implemented native dice roller for the hacking attempt.</li> <li>Simplified menus, requiring only the first letter of a menu option for menu options like [T]his.</li> <li>Switched from object-based database entries to XML-based. AkDOS.xml can be edited and is game line agnostic.</li> <li>Some code cleaning up.</li> </ul>The new XML implementation means that you can open up AkDOS.xml in Notepad (or your text editor of choice) and simply add and remove entries as you please, <b>as long as they conform to the existing hierarchy</b>. This means you can simply have one entry, or add 50 more, just make sure the tags are all there for each entry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}